workedExamples.question_text:
Calculate the area of this quadrilateral block of land. The diagonal $PR$ is $28\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.8,1.6);
\coordinate (R) at (5.6,0);
\coordinate (S) at (3.6,-2.4);
\coordinate (E) at (1.8,0);
\coordinate (F) at (3.6,0);
\draw[thick] (P)--(Q)--(R)--(S)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P)--(R) (Q)--(E) (S)--(F);
\draw (E)--++(0,0.2)--++(0.2,0)--++(0,-0.2);
\draw (F)--++(0,-0.2)--++(-0.2,0)--++(0,0.2);
\path (P) node[left] {$P$} (Q) node[above] {$Q$} (R) node[right] {$R$} (S) node[below] {$S$};
\path (1.8,0.8) node[right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (3.6,-1.2) node[right] {$12\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The diagonal $PR$ is divided at the feet of two perpendicular offsets, as shown. Calculate the area of the block to the nearest square metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (1.5,0);
\coordinate (F) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (R) at (5.2,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.5,2.3);
\coordinate (S) at (3.5,-1.6);
\draw[thick] (P)--(Q)--(R)--(S)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P)--(R) (Q)--(E) (S)--(F);
\draw (E)--++(0,0.2)--++(0.2,0)--++(0,-0.2);
\draw (F)--++(0,-0.2)--++(-0.2,0)--++(0,0.2);
\path (P) node[left] {$P$} (Q) node[above] {$Q$} (R) node[right] {$R$} (S) node[below] {$S$};
\path (E) node[below left] {$E$} (F) node[below right,xshift=3mm,yshift=-3mm] {$F$};
\path (0.75,0) node[above] {$11.5\text{ m}$};
\path (2.5,0) node[above] {$16.2\text{ m}$};
\path (4.35,0) node[above] {$13.3\text{ m}$};
\path (1.5,1.15) node[left] {$18.6\text{ m}$};
\path (3.5,-0.8) node[right] {$12.5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of quadrilateral $PQRS$ and its perimeter to the nearest metre. The dashed lines show a diagonal and perpendicular offsets.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (1.2,0);
\coordinate (F) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.2,1.6);
\coordinate (S) at (3.2,-2.4);
\draw[thick] (P)--(Q)--(R)--(S)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P)--(R) (Q)--(E) (S)--(F);
\draw (E)--++(0,0.2)--++(0.2,0)--++(0,-0.2);
\draw (F)--++(0,-0.2)--++(-0.2,0)--++(0,0.2);
\path (P) node[left] {$P$} (Q) node[above] {$Q$} (R) node[right] {$R$} (S) node[below] {$S$};
\path (E) node[below left] {$E$} (F) node[below right,xshift=3mm,yshift=-3mm] {$F$};
\path (0.6,0) node[above] {$6\text{ m}$};
\path (2.2,0) node[above] {$10\text{ m}$};
\path (3.9,0) node[above] {$7\text{ m}$};
\path (1.2,0.8) node[left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (3.2,-1.2) node[right] {$12\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Calculate the area of this irregular quadrilateral block of land.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.25);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2.25);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.75);
\coordinate (D) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2,2.25);
\coordinate (F) at (3.5,2.25);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.8, above] {$16\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (B) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (F) node[midway, right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (E) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (F) rectangle ++(-0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of this irregular block of land.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,2.7);
\coordinate (R) at (6.6,2.7);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.5,4.8);
\coordinate (S) at (4,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2.5,2.7);
\coordinate (F) at (4,2.7);
\draw[thick] (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- (S) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (P) -- (R) node[pos=0.85, above] {$22\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$7\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (S) -- (F) node[midway, right] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (E) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (F) rectangle ++(-0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

